From 4506e1c806eeae8e8d9d19dad77bd679d668a5a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samaBR85 <sama85@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 03:00:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] input: HD Rumble and DualSense haptics through RenHDrum

Plays controller vibration through RenHDrum
(https://github.com/trzz1214/RenHDrum) when renhdrum.dll is next to the
emulator: Switch Pro Controller / Joy-Con get HD Rumble packets with a
5 ms AM/FM envelope, a wired DualSense gets the vibration as 4-channel
48 kHz audio on its haptic voice coils. Without the library, or for other
controllers, nothing changes.

- input_common/drivers/renhdrum_pad: the library is loaded at runtime
  (Common::DynamicLibrary), nothing links against it. The SDL driver only
  creates a pad per controller, ticks it from PumpEvents and offers it each
  vibration first. No SDL joystick call is made while the pad mutex is held.
- HD Rumble dialog (Controls > Vibration > HD Rumble...): on/off, wired and
  Bluetooth packet options, DualSense volume, and a per-game intensity and
  weak rumble boost. Some Switch 2 games never send amplitudes above 0.1:
  The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time peaks at 0.096 through command 214,
  Donkey Kong Bananza at 0.53.
- ENABLE_RENHDRUM (ON) builds the support. RENHDRUM_DOWNLOAD (OFF) fetches
  the v0.1.1 renhdrum.dll, SHA-256 checked, next to the executable on
  Windows. RENHDRUM_SDL_PATCHES (OFF) builds SDL3 from source with
  RenHDrum's two HD Rumble transport patches (sdl3-hdrumble).
- externals/renhdrum/renhdrum.h: the RenHDrum v0.1.1 C ABI header
  (MIT OR Apache-2.0).

Based on RenHDrum's Brontide reference patches by Three-Dola
(integrations/brontide, GPL-3.0-or-later).

